ends":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a28b19253bb7550e7a42b701dae47ec9af4c8ee0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a28b19253bb7550e7a42b701dae47ec9af4c8ee0.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 11:37AM MDT until October 23 at 2:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Western Archuleta County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthern Hinsdale County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthern La Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 200 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is occurring. Streams levels remain\nelevated due to excess runoff from earlier rainfall. Multiple road\nclosures are in effect county wide.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1137 AM MDT, local law enforcement reported heavy rain in the\nwarned area since Thursday. Flooding is ongoing in the warned\narea. Rivers are forecast to slowly recede throughout this\nafternoon\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nJohnny Pond Arroyo, Lake Creek, Shearer Creek, Florida River, Hay\nGulch, True Creek, McDermott Arroyo, Pinos River, First Fork\nPiedra River, Mud Spring Creek, Beaver Creek, North Fork Texas\nCreek, Junction Creek, Long Hollow, Fall Creek, Weasel Skin\nCreek, Tirbircio Creek, Dry Creek, Animas River, Grimes Creek,\nTaylor Creek, Plata River, Wheeler Arroyo, South Fork Texas\nCreek, West Fork Shearer Creek, Cherry Creek, First Fork Red\nCreek, Spring Creek, Salt Creek, Deadwood Creek, Castle Creek,\nLittle Bear Creek, East Creek, Red Creek, Lightner Creek, Basin\nCreek, South Fork Lightner Creek, Bear Creek, San Juan Arroyo,\nFalls Creek and Vallecito Creek.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDurango, La Plata, Falfa, Hesperus, Bondad, Breen, Mayday, Kline,\nMarvel, Redmesa and Vallecito.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T14:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cb56863c318cfe6453c4d84ef2afb4027f44e356.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cb56863c318cfe6453c4d84ef2afb4027f44e356.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T18:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 231820 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1220 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flooding is ongoing across portions of southeast Utah and southwest Colorado, and is expected to continue through Saturday. - Many rivers will experience their crest Friday or Saturday. - Isolated to scattered showers and storms are expected Friday and Sa","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T06:36:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-232200- Little Snake Forecast Area- 1235 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":null,"airgradient":null,"airnow":null,"openmeteo_aq":{"pm25":0.9,"pm10":1.5,"co":108,"no2":0.2,"so2":0.5,"o3":94,"european_aqi":37,"us_aqi":38,"time":"2026-10-23T13:00"},"usgs":{"station_id":"09123450